cover measurements; there is no scope for predicting COTS from coral or
vice-versa. Not every pair of tools exists at every level: if the
requested combination has no model, the error lists what is available.

The \code{from.metric} (and \code{from.effort}, \code{from.scars}) should be, for the
different \code{from} tools:

\describe{
\item{Manta}{\code{from.metric} is the number of COTS seen on each tow and
\code{from.scars} the number of feeding scars counted on each tow (or the
scar code). The predictor is the combined density (COTS seen plus
scars counted, per tow).}
\item{ReefScan_surface, ReefScan_deep}{\code{from.metric} is the number of COTS detected
in the images; \code{from.effort} is the number of tows it was collected
over (default one per observation). Values that share a site label are
summed, and the predictor is the density (COTS per tow).}
\item{eDNA_conc}{\code{from.metric} is the concentration of each PCR assay
(replicate); the predictor is the total concentration per assay.
Missing assays are ignored.}
\item{eDNA_prop}{\code{from.metric} is either a 0/1 detection for each sample,
or the proportion of positive samples. The proportion is taken
internally.}
\item{coral_manta}{The proportion (0-1) of hard coral cover for each tow,
or the manta ordinal category as a character (\code{"0"}, \code{"1-"}, \code{"1+"},
..., \code{"5+"}), which is converted to the category midpoint. Multiple
observations per site are averaged.}
\item{coral_surface, coral_deep}{The proportion (0-1) of hard coral cover.
Multiple observations per site are averaged.}
}

